Layout:

```js
function layout(graph, opts) {
  opts = opts || {};
  const nodeW = opts.nodeW || 152, nodeH = opts.nodeH || 38;
  const colGap = opts.colGap || 46, rowGap = opts.rowGap || 96;
  const mx = opts.marginX || 60, my = opts.marginY || 56;
  // layer = longest path to a leaf along 'depends on' direction (out edges)
  const layer = new Map();
  // compute via DFS with memo, cycle-safe via in-progress guard
  const state = new Map(); // 0 unvisited 1 in progress 2 done
  function depth(id) {
    if (state.get(id) === 2) return layer.get(id);
    if (state.get(id) === 1) return 0; // back edge: ignore
    state.set(id, 1);
    const n = graph.nodes.get(id);
    let d = 0;
    if (n.out.length) { for (const e of n.out) d = Math.max(d, depth(e.to) + 1); }
    state.set(id, 2); layer.set(id, d); return d;
  }
  for (const id of graph.nodes.keys()) depth(id);
  // group by layer
  const rows = [];
  for (const id of graph.nodes.keys()) { const L = layer.get(id); (rows[L] = rows[L] || []).push(id); }
  // order rows by barycenter of neighbors in adjacent rows, few sweeps
  const pos = new Map(); rows.forEach(r => r.forEach(id => pos.set(id, { row: rows.indexOf(r) ... })))
```

Careful: rows.indexOf inside loop is O(n²) but n=28 fine. Cleaner: iterate rows with index.

Barycenter: for row i>0 order by avg index of position in row i-1 of out-neighbors? For upper rows relative to lower? Since edges go from higher layer (dependents) to lower (dependencies): row 0 = clients (top). For each node, neighbors in row i+1 (its out/deps) and row i-1 (its in/dependents). Standard: sweep downward: for i=1..maxL: order row i by barycenter of positions in row i-1 among in-edges (dependents above). Sweep upward: for i=maxL-1..0: order by barycenter in row i+1 among out-edges. Repeat 4 times. Positions within row: index.

Coordinates: x = mx + col*(nodeW+colGap); center each row horizontally: rowWidth = count*(nodeW+colGap)-colGap; xOffset = mx + (totalWidth - rowWidth)/2. y = my + row*(nodeH+rowGap). canvasW = mx*2 + max rowWidth; canvasH = my*2 + (numRows)*(nodeH+rowGap)-rowGap.

Deterministic: yes, given iteration order of Map (insertion order) — stable.

