  mm viewBox `0 0 ${w} ${h}`; dots r = max(3, w/120)... For cw≈2200, r=3 tiny in viewBox units but scaled: displayed size = r * (210/cw) ≈ 0.29px — too small! viewBox scales down. Instead draw dots in screen coords: scale s=210/cw; cx = p.x*s etc; r=2.5. And viewport rect in screen coords: worldVisible = [(0-x)/k, (0-y)/k, vw/k, vh/k] → screen: *s. Use plain coords (no viewBox).
